      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "The purpose of this research project was to evaluate the relationship and risk factors between coronary artery disease and carotid artery stenosis(CAS), screened by duplex ultra-sonography."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "1339 patients with coronary artery disease were enrolled into this study. All patients performed carotid duplex ultra-sonography during hospitalization after coronary artery angiography."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The overall incidence of CAS was 11.8%(158/1339). Patients under older age and having history of stroke, the incidence rates were higher than other groups(P < 0.01, P = 0.02). The incidence of CAS in patients with multi-vessel lesions was higher than those of diseases involved in one vessel(χ(2) = 37.482, P < 0.01). CAS patients having left side major diseases, the incidence was higher than those of others(χ(2) = 38.93, P < 0.01). By multivariable logistic regression analysis, factors as:older age, having had history of stroke, with left side major disease and multivessel lesions etc. appeared to be independent predictors of CAS, respectively."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Patients with coronary artery diseases had higher prevalence rates for CAS when suffering from multi-vessel lesions or stenosis of left major stem. Factors as being elderly, having history of cerebro-vascular diseases were independent predictors of CAS in patients with coronary artery diseases."
        }
      ]},
